information_available_at_decision:
As of early 2024 a decision-maker knew:
- the ban had been in force since 2020;
- the WTO panel had ruled against it (under appeal);
- the government reported very large increases in nickel-product exports;
- Maluku Utara and Sulawesi Tengah recorded the fastest provincial growth;
- industry-integrated coal plants had been exempted from the new-coal ban;
- a fatal smelter explosion had occurred in Morowali;
- deforestation and flooding concerns had been reported in Halmahera Tengah.
No official regional data on employment, local incomes, pollution or health was located for this case.

game_adaptation_notes:
Direct effects apply only to the two documented estate regencies, Morowali (72.06) and Halmahera Tengah (82.02). Province-level growth (BPS) is shown as context, not distributed to other kab/kota. All magnitudes are design values:
- welfare_base: structural income from industrial employment;
- environment: cumulative land clearing and emissions pressure;
- trust;
- services: inspection and health capacity;
- fiscal_space: national revenue and enforcement cost.
No production, employment, tax, pollution or health figure is converted into a number. A new variable (e.g. industrial output) was rejected because no transparent kab-level baseline exists.
